1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:02,098
Kip: The whole city is frozen...

2
00:00:02,098 --> 00:00:03,182
and I am the only one

3
00:00:03,182 --> 00:00:04,051
who can move.

4
00:00:04,901 --> 00:00:06,331
Hooded Stranger: Not the only one, Kip.

5
00:00:12,106 --> 00:00:13,674
Narrator: Twelve hours earlier.

6
00:00:13,674 --> 00:00:15,822
Floor two hundred and fourteen.

7
00:00:15,872 --> 00:00:16,620
Mom: Kip!

8
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:18,815
The sky-bus leaves in three minutes!

9
00:00:18,865 --> 00:00:19,673
Kip: Coming!

10
00:00:19,673 --> 00:00:20,523
Toast, backpack,

11
00:00:20,523 --> 00:00:22,151
shoes... why does every morning have

12
00:00:22,151 --> 00:00:23,490
so many THINGS?

13
00:00:24,628 --> 00:00:25,753
Kip: No, no, no...

14
00:00:25,753 --> 00:00:26,700
STOP!

15
00:00:28,638 --> 00:00:29,462
Kip: ...Huh.

16
00:00:29,462 --> 00:00:30,339
The milk is just...

17
00:00:30,339 --> 00:00:31,335
hanging there.

18
00:00:31,335 --> 00:00:32,350
In the air.

19
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:33,171
Kip: Mom?

20
00:00:33,171 --> 00:00:34,121
You are stuck in the middle

21
00:00:34,121 --> 00:00:34,847
of a sip.

22
00:00:34,847 --> 00:00:35,928
Is this a prank?

23
00:00:35,928 --> 00:00:37,652
Blink twice if it is a prank.

24
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:40,418
Kip: I did not break time...

25
00:00:40,418 --> 00:00:41,145
did I?

26
00:00:41,145 --> 00:00:41,999
Okay.

27
00:00:41,999 --> 00:00:43,018
Let me just put the glass

28
00:00:43,018 --> 00:00:44,373
back under the milk...

29
00:00:44,423 --> 00:00:45,197
Kip: And...

30
00:00:45,197 --> 00:00:46,049
GO?

31
00:00:47,586 --> 00:00:49,164
Mom: Ooh, nice catch, honey.

32
00:00:49,214 --> 00:00:50,003
Kip: Thanks.

33
00:00:50,003 --> 00:00:51,050
Also, Mom?

34
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:52,766
I think I just stopped time.

35
00:00:52,816 --> 00:00:54,404
Mom: That is lovely, sweetie.

36
00:00:54,404 --> 00:00:55,513
Stop time on the way to

37
00:00:55,513 --> 00:00:56,719
the bus stop.

38
00:00:56,769 --> 00:00:57,868
Kip: This... is going to be the

39
00:00:57,868 --> 00:00:59,453
best day of my life.

40
00:00:59,878 --> 00:01:01,310
Max: Wait, wait, wait.

41
00:01:01,310 --> 00:01:02,819
You stopped time?

42
00:01:02,819 --> 00:01:04,719
Like, actually stopped it?

43
00:01:04,769 --> 00:01:05,742
Kip: Watch this.

44
00:01:05,742 --> 00:01:07,463
Pick anybody on this street.

45
00:01:07,513 --> 00:01:09,695
Max: Uh... the guy with the hot dogs.

46
00:01:14,820 --> 00:01:16,873
Kip: Sunglasses... a pigeon facing the other

47
00:01:16,873 --> 00:01:18,842
way... and one tiny mustache.

48
00:01:18,842 --> 00:01:19,888
Perfect.

49
00:01:21,225 --> 00:01:21,950
Hot-Dog Vendor: Hey!

50
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:24,023
Where did these sunglasses come from?

51
00:01:24,023 --> 00:01:25,840
...Actually, I look amazing.

52
00:01:25,890 --> 00:01:26,767
Max: WHAT?!

53
00:01:26,767 --> 00:01:27,876
Kip, you were over there,

54
00:01:27,876 --> 00:01:29,539
and now you are over HERE!

55
00:01:29,589 --> 00:01:30,094
Kip: One clap,

56
00:01:30,094 --> 00:01:31,255
everything stops.

57
00:01:31,255 --> 00:01:31,790
Two claps,

58
00:01:31,790 --> 00:01:32,894
everything goes.

59
00:01:32,894 --> 00:01:34,654
I practised on the sky-bus.

60
00:01:34,704 --> 00:01:36,152
Max: This is huge!

61
00:01:36,152 --> 00:01:38,040
You could skip every test!

62
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:39,394
You could be first in every

63
00:01:39,394 --> 00:01:40,542
lunch line!

64
00:01:40,592 --> 00:01:42,087
Kip: Or... we could go to Starlight

65
00:01:42,087 --> 00:01:43,737
Mall and try every free sample

66
00:01:43,737 --> 00:01:45,292
at the same time.

67
00:01:45,342 --> 00:01:46,112
Max: Kip.

68
00:01:46,112 --> 00:01:47,889
You are a genius.

69
00:01:47,939 --> 00:01:50,224
Max: Why does my face feel tickly?

70
00:01:52,637 --> 00:01:54,283
Mall Speaker: Welcome to Starlight Mall!

71
00:01:54,283 --> 00:01:55,051
Today only:

72
00:01:55,051 --> 00:01:57,848
free robot-baked cookies on every level!

73
00:01:57,898 --> 00:01:58,693
Kip: Ready?

74
00:01:58,693 --> 00:01:59,977
Three, two, one...

75
00:02:01,515 --> 00:02:02,339
Kip: Max?

76
00:02:02,339 --> 00:02:03,414
Max! ...Oh.

77
00:02:03,414 --> 00:02:04,188
Right.

78
00:02:04,188 --> 00:02:05,498
You freeze too.

79
00:02:07,536 --> 00:02:09,141
Kip: The fountain stopped in mid-air.

80
00:02:09,141 --> 00:02:10,548
That is so beautiful.

81
00:02:10,598 --> 00:02:11,608
Kip: Free cookie.

82
00:02:11,608 --> 00:02:12,618
Free cookie.

83
00:02:12,618 --> 00:02:13,615
Free smoothie.

84
00:02:13,615 --> 00:02:14,540
I am leaving a coin,

85
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:15,929
I am not a criminal.

86
00:02:17,366 --> 00:02:18,173
Kip: Uh oh.

87
00:02:18,173 --> 00:02:19,659
Somebody lost a balloon.

88
00:02:19,659 --> 00:02:21,050
Let me just tie that back

89
00:02:21,050 --> 00:02:22,490
on... extra tight.

90
00:02:25,328 --> 00:02:26,090
Kip: Wait.

91
00:02:26,090 --> 00:02:27,688
That person on the escalator.

92
00:02:27,688 --> 00:02:29,058
They are... moving.

93
00:02:29,108 --> 00:02:29,880
Kip: Hello?

94
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:31,470
Are you freeze-proof too?

95
00:02:33,307 --> 00:02:34,161
Kip: Okay.

96
00:02:34,161 --> 00:02:34,952
Nope.

97
00:02:34,952 --> 00:02:36,290
Nope, nope, nope.

98
00:02:37,627 --> 00:02:38,454
Max: Whoa.

99
00:02:38,454 --> 00:02:40,748
Why am I holding three cookies?

100
00:02:40,798 --> 00:02:42,111
Little Girl: Mommy, look!

101
00:02:42,111 --> 00:02:44,722
My balloon is tied on super tight!

102
00:02:44,772 --> 00:02:46,442
Kip: Max, somebody else was moving.

103
00:02:46,442 --> 00:02:47,985
While everything was stopped.

104
00:02:48,035 --> 00:02:49,918
Max: Like a time ninja?

105
00:02:49,968 --> 00:02:51,118
Kip: Like a time ninja who was

106
00:02:51,118 --> 00:02:52,658
looking right at me.

107
00:02:53,083 --> 00:02:54,623
Max: Okay, theory.

108
00:02:54,623 --> 00:02:56,884
Maybe it was just a reflection.

109
00:02:56,934 --> 00:02:59,125
Kip: Reflections do not wear hoods, Max.

110
00:02:59,175 --> 00:02:59,991
Kip: I need to know if they

111
00:02:59,991 --> 00:03:00,726
are real.

112
00:03:00,726 --> 00:03:01,940
One more time.

113
00:03:01,990 --> 00:03:03,826
Max: Kip, maybe do not...

114
00:03:05,463 --> 00:03:06,231
Kip: Whoa.

115
00:03:06,231 --> 00:03:07,622
Even the rain stopped.

116
00:03:07,622 --> 00:03:09,274
I can walk right through it.

117
00:03:09,324 --> 00:03:10,773
Kip: The whole city is frozen...

118
00:03:10,773 --> 00:03:11,857
and I am the only one

119
00:03:11,857 --> 00:03:13,113
who can move.

120
00:03:15,051 --> 00:03:16,047
Kip: What is THAT?

121
00:03:16,047 --> 00:03:17,539
Is the air... cracked?

122
00:03:18,526 --> 00:03:20,343
Hooded Stranger: Not the only one, Kip.

123
00:03:20,393 --> 00:03:21,328
Kip: Who are you?

124
00:03:21,328 --> 00:03:22,879
Why are you following me?!

125
00:03:22,929 --> 00:03:24,548
Hooded Stranger: Every second you freeze is stolen

126
00:03:24,548 --> 00:03:25,791
from the future.

127
00:03:25,791 --> 00:03:27,906
And the future always collects.

128
00:03:27,956 --> 00:03:28,810
Kip: Okay.

129
00:03:28,810 --> 00:03:30,331
That is the creepiest thing anyone

130
00:03:30,331 --> 00:03:31,811
has ever said to me.

131
00:03:31,861 --> 00:03:33,597
Hooded Stranger: Give me your hands, Kip.

132
00:03:33,597 --> 00:03:35,450
Before it is too late.

133
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:36,921
Kip: Absolutely not!

134
00:03:39,734 --> 00:03:40,793
Kip: Sorry, Max!

135
00:03:40,793 --> 00:03:42,232
You are coming with me!

136
00:03:44,869 --> 00:03:45,726
Kip: Frozen people,

137
00:03:45,726 --> 00:03:46,681
frozen people...

138
00:03:46,681 --> 00:03:47,439
sorry, sir!

139
00:03:47,439 --> 00:03:49,363
...Why are you so heavy, Max?!

140
00:03:51,401 --> 00:03:52,153
Kip: Clap!

141
00:03:52,153 --> 00:03:53,042
Clap!

142
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:56,183
Station Speaker: Doors closing.

143
00:03:56,183 --> 00:03:59,211
Line Nine to Chrono District.

144
00:03:59,261 --> 00:04:00,542
Max: ...not do that.

145
00:04:00,542 --> 00:04:01,409
Wait.

146
00:04:01,409 --> 00:04:03,326
Why are we on a train?

147
00:04:03,376 --> 00:04:04,395
Kip: Long story.

148
00:04:04,395 --> 00:04:05,910
Very creepy story.

149
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:07,782
Max: Kip... is that your ninja?

150
00:04:07,782 --> 00:04:09,300
On the platform?

151
00:04:11,538 --> 00:04:13,599
Kip: The train is going to Chrono District.

152
00:04:13,599 --> 00:04:15,780
Where the famous time scientist works.

153
00:04:15,830 --> 00:04:17,331
Max: Professor Tock?

154
00:04:17,331 --> 00:04:18,931
From the science show?

155
00:04:18,931 --> 00:04:20,349
Let us go!

156
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:23,925
Professor Tock: Visitors!

157
00:04:23,925 --> 00:04:26,628
Do not touch anything that glows.

158
00:04:26,628 --> 00:04:27,809
Or hums.

159
00:04:27,809 --> 00:04:30,321
Actually, do not touch anything.

160
00:04:30,371 --> 00:04:32,365
Kip: Professor, I think I can stop time.

161
00:04:32,365 --> 00:04:33,415
And someone in a hood can

162
00:04:33,415 --> 00:04:34,729
move when I do it.

163
00:04:34,779 --> 00:04:36,093
Professor Tock: Stop time?

164
00:04:36,093 --> 00:04:37,031
Ha!

165
00:04:37,031 --> 00:04:38,306
Impossible.

166
00:04:38,306 --> 00:04:40,066
Unless... were you near this building

167
00:04:40,066 --> 00:04:41,251
last night?

168
00:04:41,301 --> 00:04:42,294
Kip: I walked past here on the

169
00:04:42,294 --> 00:04:43,070
way home.

170
00:04:43,070 --> 00:04:44,828
There was a big purple flash.

171
00:04:44,878 --> 00:04:46,585
Professor Tock: My Chrono Pulse!

172
00:04:46,585 --> 00:04:48,592
It soaked right into you!

173
00:04:48,592 --> 00:04:49,836
Remarkable!

174
00:04:49,836 --> 00:04:50,913
Terrible!

175
00:04:50,913 --> 00:04:52,709
Mostly terrible!

176
00:04:52,759 --> 00:04:54,179
Max: Why terrible?

177
00:04:54,229 --> 00:04:56,764
Professor Tock: Time is like ice on a lake.

178
00:04:56,764 --> 00:04:58,204
Every time you freeze it,

179
00:04:58,204 --> 00:04:59,824
it cracks a little.

180
00:04:59,874 --> 00:05:01,023
Professor Tock: Too many cracks...

181
00:05:01,023 --> 00:05:02,370
and time stops.

182
00:05:02,370 --> 00:05:03,423
Forever.

183
00:05:03,423 --> 00:05:04,855
For everyone.

184
00:05:04,905 --> 00:05:05,675
Max: Kip.

185
00:05:05,675 --> 00:05:07,128
How many times did you freeze

186
00:05:07,128 --> 00:05:08,186
it today?

187
00:05:08,236 --> 00:05:10,325
Kip: Um... counting the pigeon and the balloon?

188
00:05:10,325 --> 00:05:11,324
Eleven.

189
00:05:11,374 --> 00:05:12,640
Professor Tock: ELEVEN?!

190
00:05:14,178 --> 00:05:15,494
Hooded Stranger: Twelve.

191
00:05:15,494 --> 00:05:17,245
If you count the milk.

192
00:05:17,295 --> 00:05:18,347
Kip: It is YOU!

193
00:05:20,984 --> 00:05:21,996
Professor Tock: Wren?!

194
00:05:21,996 --> 00:05:23,253
My daughter?

195
00:05:23,253 --> 00:05:25,808
You disappeared a year ago!

196
00:05:25,858 --> 00:05:27,456
Wren: I never left, Dad.

197
00:05:27,456 --> 00:05:29,485
Your first Chrono Pulse hit me.

198
00:05:29,485 --> 00:05:31,726
I have been living between the seconds.

199
00:05:31,776 --> 00:05:33,701
Wren: I followed you to stop you, Kip.

200
00:05:33,701 --> 00:05:35,122
Not to hurt you.

201
00:05:35,122 --> 00:05:37,173
The cracks are almost joined.

202
00:05:37,223 --> 00:05:38,269
Kip: Then why did you not just

203
00:05:38,269 --> 00:05:39,210
SAY that?

204
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:40,439
Wren: I tried.

205
00:05:40,439 --> 00:05:42,098
You screamed and dragged your friend

206
00:05:42,098 --> 00:05:43,294
onto a train.

207
00:05:43,344 --> 00:05:44,724
Max: He did WHAT?

208
00:05:46,361 --> 00:05:48,014
Professor Tock: The crack monitor!

209
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:49,547
They are joining up!

210
00:05:49,547 --> 00:05:51,876
Everybody hold on to some...

211
00:05:54,514 --> 00:05:55,533
Kip: Clap, clap!

212
00:05:55,533 --> 00:05:56,552
CLAP, CLAP!

213
00:05:56,552 --> 00:05:58,023
Why is it not working?!

214
00:05:58,073 --> 00:06:00,512
Wren: Because time is not paused anymore, Kip.

215
00:06:00,512 --> 00:06:02,162
It is broken.

216
00:06:05,175 --> 00:06:06,414
Wren: The Chrono Core is on top

217
00:06:06,414 --> 00:06:07,748
of the Tock Tower.

218
00:06:07,748 --> 00:06:08,749
If we both touch it,

219
00:06:08,749 --> 00:06:10,256
the cracks will heal.

220
00:06:10,306 --> 00:06:11,304
Kip: Then why do you sound sad

221
00:06:11,304 --> 00:06:12,220
about it?

222
00:06:12,270 --> 00:06:13,774
Wren: Because the Core takes back all

223
00:06:13,774 --> 00:06:15,003
the stolen time.

224
00:06:15,003 --> 00:06:16,829
And our power goes with it.

225
00:06:16,829 --> 00:06:17,930
Forever.

226
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:18,717
Kip: So I would be...

227
00:06:18,717 --> 00:06:19,789
normal again.

228
00:06:19,839 --> 00:06:21,280
Wren: Normal.

229
00:06:21,280 --> 00:06:22,668
Late for the bus.

230
00:06:22,668 --> 00:06:24,230
Spilling the milk.

231
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:25,200
Kip: Honestly?

232
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:26,666
I kind of miss normal.

233
00:06:28,503 --> 00:06:30,508
Wren: The street is falling apart!

234
00:06:30,508 --> 00:06:32,382
Jump on the hover-cars!

235
00:06:32,432 --> 00:06:33,741
Kip: Falling APART?!

236
00:06:37,379 --> 00:06:38,422
Kip: I am okay!

237
00:06:38,422 --> 00:06:39,466
I am okay!

238
00:06:39,466 --> 00:06:40,762
I am standing on a frozen

239
00:06:40,762 --> 00:06:42,437
pigeon, but I am okay!

240
00:06:42,487 --> 00:06:43,672
Wren: Keep going!

241
00:06:43,672 --> 00:06:45,379
Up the sky-stairs!

242
00:06:48,192 --> 00:06:49,362
Wren: There it is.

243
00:06:49,362 --> 00:06:50,585
Ready?

244
00:06:50,585 --> 00:06:51,832
On three.

245
00:06:51,882 --> 00:06:52,644
Kip: Wait.

246
00:06:52,644 --> 00:06:53,576
Wren... if we do this,

247
00:06:53,576 --> 00:06:55,041
you lose your power too.

248
00:06:55,041 --> 00:06:55,787
You have had it for a

249
00:06:55,787 --> 00:06:56,702
whole year.

250
00:06:56,752 --> 00:06:58,116
Wren: A whole year as the only

251
00:06:58,116 --> 00:07:00,302
person awake in a frozen world.

252
00:07:00,302 --> 00:07:01,695
Trust me, Kip.

253
00:07:01,695 --> 00:07:03,259
It gets lonely.

254
00:07:03,309 --> 00:07:04,534
Kip: Then let us go back.

255
00:07:04,534 --> 00:07:05,388
Together.

256
00:07:05,388 --> 00:07:06,310
One...

257
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:07,471
Wren: Two...

258
00:07:07,521 --> 00:07:08,418
Everyone: THREE!

259
00:07:13,143 --> 00:07:14,604
Professor Tock: ...thing! ...Oh.

260
00:07:14,604 --> 00:07:15,670
Hello.

261
00:07:15,670 --> 00:07:17,921
Did something just happen?

262
00:07:17,971 --> 00:07:18,766
Max: Kip!

263
00:07:18,766 --> 00:07:19,709
You were over there,

264
00:07:19,709 --> 00:07:21,235
and now you are over here!

265
00:07:21,235 --> 00:07:22,343
AGAIN!

266
00:07:22,393 --> 00:07:24,112
Kip: Max, I will explain everything.

267
00:07:24,112 --> 00:07:25,030
Mostly.

268
00:07:25,030 --> 00:07:25,987
Some of it.

269
00:07:25,987 --> 00:07:27,215
Over pizza.

270
00:07:27,265 --> 00:07:28,425
Wren: Hi, Dad.

271
00:07:28,425 --> 00:07:29,661
I am back.

272
00:07:29,661 --> 00:07:31,398
For real this time.

273
00:07:31,448 --> 00:07:32,743
Professor Tock: Oh, Wren.

274
00:07:32,743 --> 00:07:33,697
A whole year...

275
00:07:33,697 --> 00:07:35,711
and you have not aged a day.

276
00:07:35,711 --> 00:07:37,792
Well, you have aged a year.

277
00:07:37,792 --> 00:07:39,650
You know what I mean.

278
00:07:41,488 --> 00:07:42,438
Kip: It is gone.

279
00:07:42,438 --> 00:07:43,339
I am just a kid who

280
00:07:43,339 --> 00:07:44,382
claps now.

281
00:07:44,432 --> 00:07:45,684
Max: Kip, you were always a kid

282
00:07:45,684 --> 00:07:46,843
who claps.

283
00:07:47,269 --> 00:07:48,401
Kip: A brand-new day.

284
00:07:48,401 --> 00:07:49,495
No powers.

285
00:07:49,495 --> 00:07:50,525
No cracks.

286
00:07:50,525 --> 00:07:52,965
Just a perfectly normal sky-bus ride.

287
00:07:53,015 --> 00:07:54,681
Max: Yeah... about normal.

288
